I reviewed the section. It's an ORM parameter adapter that converts spatial objects (geometry or GDALRaster) into SQL string literals. There's no user-controlled object identifier, no request context, and no authentication/authorization surface involved. The `to_pgraster` helper operates on a `GDALRaster` object (attribute access like `rast.bands`, `rast.scale.x`), so the non-geometry branch requires an actual GDALRaster instance to work — not a raw user string. This change doesn't introduce, modify, or remove any authorization logic.

No authorization-flaw policy in the docs applies to ORM parameter adapters, and no changed line cites a missing/wrong authorization check.

