The changes are all within spatial query compilation (SQL generation for GIS lookups): extracting band indices, rejecting raster for `isvalid`, and accepting 4-element distance tuples. No object fetch by user-controlled identifier, no authentication/permission enforcement point, no role checks — this is ORM SQL-compilation code, not an authorization boundary. The retrieved policy excerpts concern admin querystring lookup whitelisting and custom auth backends, which do not apply to this internal GIS lookup mechanism, and there is no policy rule governing band-index/lookup validation here.

No authorization (CWE-639/862/863) flaw is introduced or newly exposed by these changed lines.

