}

The only dynamically-constructed SQL text in the changed code is the raster branch `return "'%s'::raster" % self.ewkb` (adapter.py line 68). However, `self.ewkb` comes from `to_pgraster(rast)`, which produces an uppercase hex string via `binascii.hexlify(...).upper()`, and the final `result.decode()` (pgraster.py lines 13-16, 155, 161). Since the value is constrained to the hex alphabet [0-9A-F], it can never contain a quote or inject SQL. The geometry branch is unchanged and uses psycopg2 `Binary` for safe quoting. No attacker-controlled value reaches unbound/unchecked SQL text.

