The band indices are injected directly into SQL text via string formatting in `check_raster`. `band_lhs` is derived from `self.lhs.band_index`, which comes from `RasterField.get_transform` — the value is passed through `int(name)`, so it is coerced to a Python int and cannot be attacker-influenced. `band_rhs` is set to `self.rhs[1]` (a user-supplied lookup value, e.g. `filter(raster__band=(raster, 5)`), and is concatenated directly into the SQL text at operations.py:66 without binding. That value reaches the executed SQL as a numeric literal and is not validated against a numeric type.

